<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucRegulation_lblGoalDescription">Describe your lobbying goal(s) in detail.  What are you attempting to influence or accomplish as a result of your communications with Ontario public office holders?</span></p>
<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucRegulation_txtGoalDescription">Advocate for policies that maintain a competitive carbon pricing framework for Ontario industries, including alignment with federal carbon pricing systems and measures that prevent carbon leakage and ensure Ontario-based low-carbon fuel producers remain competitive with imported fuels produced under different regulatory regimes.
Maintain support of the April 18, 2018/November 2020 amendments to the Ministry of the Environment, Conservation and Park regulation (O. Reg 535/05) requiring fuel suppliers to maintain at least an annual average of 10% renewable content (such as ethanol) in the gasoline they sell in Ontario starting in 2020. Promote and incent the production and deployment of renewable natural gas, low carbon hydrogen and methanol in Ontario.</span></p>
