<p><img id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_imgHelpPolicyProgram" class="ux-img-valign " src="../../../Stylesheets/Images/help_0.gif">
<span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblPolicyProgram">Policy and/or program</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<b><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_lblPolicyProgramAnswer">Yes</span></b></p>

<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucPolicyProgram_lblGoalDescription">Describe your lobbying goal(s) in detail.  What are you attempting to influence or accomplish as a result of your communications with Ontario public office holders?</span></p>
<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucPolicyProgram_txtGoalDescription">As the leading biofuels and specialty alcohols manufacturer in Ontario, Greenfield will advocate for the effective implementation of low carbon fuels contemplated under the Made-in-Ontario Environment Plan.  As an advanced biofuels technology provider, Greenfield will advocate for the funding to commercialize our technology, both locally and globally. Support policies that strengthen Ontario’s domestic supply chain for agricultural-based fermentation products, including ethanol and beverage alcohol inputs, in order to support Ontario farmers, maintain domestic production capacity, and ensure reliable supply for food, beverage, and fuel markets.
Maintain and improve the standing of Ontario as an ethanol and biofuels-friendly jurisdiction. Promote the commercialization of next-generation biofuels and low-carbon fuels in Ontario, including renewable natural gas produced through anaerobic digestion, low-carbon hydrogen and methanol and sustainable aviation fuel. Support policies that strengthen Ontario’s agricultural bioeconomy, create value from agricultural by-products and organic waste streams, and expand domestic supply chains for fuel ethanol and fermentation-based industries.</span></p>
