<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucGrantContribution_lblGoalDescription">Describe your lobbying goal(s) in detail.  What are you attempting to influence or accomplish as a result of your communications with Ontario public office holders?</span></p>
<p><span id="BodyContent_ucRegistrationSubmit_LobbyingActivity_ucGrantContribution_txtGoalDescription">As the leading biofuels manufacturer in Ontario, Greenfield will advocate for the effective implementation of low carbon fuels contemplated under the Made-in-Ontario Environment Plan. As an advanced biofuels technology provider, Greenfield will advocate for the funding to commercialize our technology, both locally and globally. Support policies and programs that position Ontario as a leader in the bioeconomy by encouraging investment in low-carbon fuels and technologies including industrial fermentation and agricultural processing that create rural economic development and strengthen Ontario supply chains.
To access existing and new funding programs and taxation policy to create an Advanced Biofuels cluster in the province of Ontario. Government regulations and programs that will incent the commercialization of renewable natural gas, low carbon hydrogen, methanol and sustainable aviation fuel for use in the province of Ontario and to meet growing demand both nationally and globally.</span></p>
